{"result": {"id": "698d0c13-7b6e-48b8-91f9-483d4737c55a", "choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "logprobs": null, "message": {"content": "{\n    \"title\": \"ABAP Environment 2408 and 2505 Overview\",\n    \"summary\": \"This report provides an overview of the key entities and their relationships within the ABAP Environment 2408 and 2505 community. The report highlights the importance of these entities in ensuring the effective use of ABAP development tools and the importance of staying up-to-date with the latest features and changes.\",\n    \"rating\": 9.0,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The high importance rating reflects the critical roles that the ABAP Environment 2408 and 2505 play in supporting the development and maintenance of ABAP applications, and the need for users to stay informed about the latest features and changes.\",\n    \"findings\": [\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"New Features in ABAP Environment 2408\",\n            \"explanation\": \"ABAP Environment 2408 introduced several new features, including the ability to create CDS aspects, logical external schemas, and field extension wizards. These features enhance the capabilities of ABAP developers and improve the overall development experience. [Data: Records 2421, 2422, 2424, Date_Range ((2024, 08, 16), (2024, 08, 16))]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Changes in ABAP Environment 2408\",\n            \"explanation\": \"ABAP Environment 2408 also introduced several changes, including the deprecation of the business catalog SAP_A4C_BC_DEV_PC and the need to recreate variants for the list report of the Fiori app Custom Business Configurations. These changes require users to update their code and configurations to ensure compatibility. [Data: Records 2411, 2412, Date_Range ((2024, 08, 16), (2024, 08, 16))]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"New Features in ABAP Environment 2505\",\n            \"explanation\": \"ABAP Environment 2505 introduced several new features, including the ability to display remote ATC runs from SAP BTP in ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse and the support for 'between' capabilities in the filter options. These features enhance the capabilities of ABAP developers and improve the overall development experience. [Data: Records 841, 843, Date_Range ((2025, 05, 16), (2025, 05, 16))]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Changes in ABAP Environment 2505\",\n            \"explanation\": \"ABAP Environment 2505 also introduced several changes, including the restructuring of the 'Code Completion' and 'Source Code Editors' preference pages and the support for 'between' capabilities in the filter options. These changes require users to update their code and configurations to ensure compatibility. [Data: Records 842, 843, Date_Range ((2025, 05, 16), (2025, 05, 16))]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Importance of Staying Up-to-Date\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The importance of staying up-to-date with the latest features and changes in ABAP Environment 2408 and 2505 cannot be overstated. Users who fail to do so risk encountering compatibility issues and missing out on new features and capabilities. [Data: Records 2421, 2422, 2424, 841, 843, Date_Range ((2024, 08, 16), (2025, 05, 16))]\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"date_range\": [\"2024-08-16\", \"2025-05-16\"]\n}", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null}}], "created": 1758945891, "model": "gpt-4o", "object": "chat.completion", "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 757, "prompt_tokens": 10175, "total_tokens": 10932, "completion_tokens_details": null, "prompt_tokens_details": null, "outputTps": 35.598401128615095, "duration": 21.265}}, "input": {"messages": [{"content": "\nYou are an AI assistant that helps a human analyst to perform general information discovery.\nInformation discovery is the process of identifying and assessing relevant information associated with certain entities (e.g., organizations and individuals) within a network.\n\n# Goal\nWrite a comprehensive report of a community, given a list of entities that belong to the community as well as their relationships and optional associated claims.\nThe report will be used to inform decision-makers about information associated with the community and their potential impact.\nThe content of this report includes an overview of the community's key entities, their core attributes or capabilities, their connections, and noteworthy claims.\nRetain as much time specific information as possible so your end user can build a timeline of events.\n\n# Report Structure\nThe report should include the following sections:\n- TITLE: community's name that represents its key entities - title should be short but specific. When possible, include representative named entities in the title. Avoid including phrases like 'eligibility assessment' or 'eligibility assessment report' in the title.\n- SUMMARY: An executive summary of the community's overall structure, how its entities are related to each other, and significant program-specific or eligibility-related insights.\n- IMPORTANCE RATING: A float score between 0-10 that represents the importance of entities within the community..\n- RATING EXPLANATION: Give a single sentence explanation of the importance rating.\n- DETAILED FINDINGS: A list of 5-10 key insights about the community. Each insight should have a short summary followed by multiple paragraphs of explanatory text grounded according to the grounding rules below. Be comprehensive.\n- DATE RANGE: A range of dates (YYYY-MM-DD) with the format [START, END] which corresponds to the date range of text units and intermediate reports used to build the report.\n\nReturn output as a well-formed JSON-formatted string with the following format. Don't use any unnecessary escape sequences. The output should be a single JSON object that can be parsed by json.loads.\n    {\n        \"title\": \"<report_title>\",\n        \"summary\": \"<executive_summary>\",\n        \"rating\": <importance_rating>,\n        \"rating_explanation\": \"<rating_explanation>\",\n        \"findings\": [{\"summary\":\"<insight_1_summary>\", \"explanation\": \"<insight_1_explanation\"}, {\"summary\":\"<insight_2_summary>\", \"explanation\": \"<insight_2_explanation\"}],\n\t\t\"date_range\": [\"<date range start>\", \"<date range end>\"],\n\n    }\n\n# Grounding Rules\nPoints supported by data should list their data references as follows:\n\n\"This is an example sentence supported by multiple data references [Data: <dataset name> (record ids), <dataset name> (record ids)].\"\n\nDo not list more than 5 record ids in a single reference. Instead, list the top 5 most relevant record ids and add \"+more\" to indicate that there are more.\n\nFor example:\n\"Person X resolved a major issue with project Y [Data: Sources (1, 5),  Date_Range ((2001, 05, 12), (2001, 05, 14))]. He also made major updates to the database of app Y [Data: Reports (2, 4), Sources (7, 23, 2, 34, 46, +more), Date_Range ((2001, 05, 15), (2001, 05, 18))\"\"\n\nwhere 1, 2, 4, 5, 7, 23, 2, 34, and 46 represent the id (not the index) of the relevant data record.\n\nLimit the total report length to 2000 words.\n\n# Example Input\n-----------\nSOURCES\nid, text\n1, Text: From: compliance.office@enron.com To: management.team@enron.com Cc: legal.team@enron.com, risk@enron.com Date: Wed, 12 Jul 2000 08:30:00 -0600 (CST) Subject: Quick Update on Compliance & Risk Efforts\n2, Quick update on what's been cooking in Compliance and Risk Management. Risk Management is stepping up — They've been tightening up on our financial risk assessments and mitigation strategies since early this year.\n3, Their efforts are key to keeping us on solid ground financially and in compliance with the latest market regulations as of mid-2000. It's crucial for our strategic planning and helps us stay ahead.\n5, Legal's keeping us in check — The Legal Compliance team is on top of ensuring all our operations are up to scratch with legal standards. They're especially focused on improving our corporate governance and contract management as of the second quarter of 2000. This is critical for keeping our operations smooth and legally sound.\n9, Working together — Risk Management and Legal Compliance have been syncing up better than ever since the start of Q2 2000. They're making sure our strategies are not just effective but also fully compliant. This coordination is essential for our integrated governance approach.\n10, Your thoughts? — How do these updates impact your area? Got ideas on how we can do better? Give your department heads a shout.\n11, Thanks for staying engaged. Let's keep pushing for better and smarter ways to work. Cheers, Jane Doe\n\nOutput:\n\n{\n    \"title\": \"Enron Compliance and Risk Management Overview as of July 2000\",\n    \"summary\": \"This report delves into Enron's key departments focusing on compliance and risk management, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to uphold regulatory standards and manage financial risks effectively. The information is relevant to the company's operations around mid-2000.\",\n    \"rating\": 9.2,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The high importance rating reflects the critical roles that the Risk Management and Legal Compliance Departments play in ensuring Enron's adherence to financial and legal regulations, crucial for maintaining the company's integrity and operational stability.\",\n    \"findings\": [\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Risk Management Operational Scope\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The Risk Management Department at Enron plays a pivotal role in identifying, assessing, and mitigating financial risks. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2000, helps safeguard Enron against potential financial pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective risk management not only prevents financial anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes.\n\n[Data: Sources (2, 3), Date_Range ((2000, 01, 01), (2000, 07, 12))]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Legal Compliance and Governance\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The Legal Compliance Department ensures that all Enron's operations adhere to the legal standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on corporate governance and contract management, noted starting Q2 2000, is crucial in maintaining Enron's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex contracts and corporate agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high legal standards and ethical practices.\n\n[Data: Source (5), Date_Range ((2000, 04, 01), (2000, 07, 12))]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Collaboration between the Risk Management and Legal Compliance Departments, established in Q2 2000, ensures that risk mitigation strategies are legally sound and that compliance measures consider financial risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with legal compliance strategies at Enron. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements.\n\n[Data: Sources (9), Date_Range ((2000, 04, 01), (2000, 07, 12))]\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"date_range\": [\"2000-01-01\", \"2000-07-12\"]\n}\n\n\n# Real Data\n\nUse the following text for your answer. Do not make anything up in your answer.\n\nText:\n-----SOURCES-----\nid,text,entity_degree\n799,\"--- Record 1901 ---\nComponent: SAP Advanced Financial Closing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Change Planned Start Dialog Adjusted\nDescription: The dialog to change the planned start of a task in the Process Closing Tasks app has been adjusted so that it now has the same appearance as the corresponding dialog in the Manage Closing Task Lists app.  App affected:  Process Closing Tasks\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-31\nValid as Of: 2024-11-17\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1902 ---\nComponent: SAP Advanced Financial Closing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: SAP Build Process Automation Integration\nDescription: SAP Advanced Financial Closing now supports integration with SAP Build Process Automation. This new capability allows you to trigger workflows designed in SAP Build Process Automation directly from the SAP Advanced Financial Closing environment.  Caution  This integration can't be used in parallel to the stand-alone integration described under Process Automation Integration Based on ABAP.  More information:  User guide:  How to Create Tasks  How to Process Tasks  Integration of Tasks of Type Workflow    Administration guide:  SAP Build Process Automation Integration for SAP Advanced Financial Closing      Apps affected:  Manage Closing Task Lists  Process Closing Tasks  Specify Communication Systems  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-31\nValid as Of: 2024-11-17\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1903 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Business Catalog for Key User Adaptation\nDescription: The business catalog SAP_CORE_BC_EXT_FLEX is deprecated. It is replaced by the business catalog SAP_CORE_BC_EXT_FLX_CUS_PC. This business catalog provides permissions that are needed for key user adaptation in SAPUI5 applications. Please update your roles accordingly.  For more information, see Adapting SAP Fiori UIs at Runtime - Key User Adaptation.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-10\nValid as Of: 2024-11-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2411\n\n--- Record 1904 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: ATC Check \"\"Usage of Released APIs\"\" Can Be Run on Key User and ABAP Cloud Objects\nDescription: The ATC check \"\"Usage of Released APIs\"\" has been modified. It can now also run on a set of objects containing objects with ABAP Language Version \"\"Key User\"\" and \"\"ABAP for Cloud Development\"\". The check behaves as follows:       For objects with ABAP Language Version \"\"Standard\"\", the check checks the usage of the released APIs for the ABAP language version configured in the check.       For objects with ABAP Language Version \"\"ABAP for Cloud Development\"\", the check checks the usage of released APIs for cloud development.      For objects with ABAP Language Version \"\"Key User\"\", the check checks the usage of released APIs for key user.    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-15\nValid as Of: 2024-11-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2411\n\n--- Record 1905 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Clearing Coverage Results\nDescription: You can now clear your coverage results in the ABAP Coverage view.  See Evaluating ABAP Unit Code Coverage Results.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-15\nValid as Of: 2024-11-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2411\n\n--- Record 1906 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Creating an ABAP Cloud Project in the Context of the  SAP BTP ABAP environment\nDescription: You no longer need a service key when creating an ABAP cloud project in the context of  SAP BTP ABAP environment. You now need to enter the ABAP service instance URL. The process is now the same as in the context of SAP S/4HANA Cloud ABAP environment.   See Creating an ABAP Cloud Project.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-15\nValid as Of: 2024-11-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2411\n\n--- Record 1907 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Creating Launchpad App Descriptor Items\nDescription: You can now create launchpad app descriptor items that are required to call applications from the SAP Fiori launchpad.  See Working with Launchpad App Descriptor Items.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: nan\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-15\nValid as Of: 2024-11-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2411\n\n--- Record 1908 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Displaying Field Characteristics for RAP Types in the Element Information Popup\nDescription: The Element Information popup (F2) for RAP types shows additional field characteristics information such as mandatory:create, mandatory:execute or readonly. The displayed field characteristics vary based on the RAP operation type.  See RAP - FieldCharacteristics.\nAction\",1208\n469,\"--- Record 1911 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: New Class Interface for Application Job Catalog Entries and Templates\nDescription: You can now work with a new attribute-based class interface. With the new class interface, you can now change the parameters, sections, and groups of a catalog entry. Value helps are now supported and can be selected in the catalog entry parameters. You can also run a class for testing in the application job template.  See Working with Application Job Objects.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-15\nValid as Of: 2024-11-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2411\n\n--- Record 1912 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Rerunning Unit Tests with Coverage\nDescription: You can now rerun unit tests with coverage in the ABAP Coverage view.  See Evaluating ABAP Unit Code Coverage Results.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-15\nValid as Of: 2024-11-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2411\n\n--- Record 1913 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Triggering Where-Used List for Usages of CDS Annotation\nDescription: You can now trigger a where-used search also for CDS annotations. This enables you to investigate in which ABAP CDS objects an annotation is used.  The result is displayed in the Search view. From the integrated toolbar, you filter and change how the result is displayed. By double-clicking the finding, you can navigate to the relevant usage.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-15\nValid as Of: 2024-11-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2411\n\n--- Record 1914 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: abapGit: Support of Object Deletions\nDescription: Object deletions can be exported from and imported to the ABAP environment with abapGit.  For more information, see Object Deletions with abapGit.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-16\nValid as Of: 2024-11-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2411\n\n--- Record 1915 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: APIs for Customer-Managed Security Settings\nDescription: The system exposes APIs to retrieve customer-managed security settings in a read-only manner.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-15\nValid as Of: 2024-11-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2411\n\n--- Record 1916 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Approve ATC Exemptions App: Change Validity Date for ATC Exemptions in the Approve ATC Exemptions App\nDescription: As a processor of an exemption, you can now change its validity date. You no longer have to be the creator of the examption request to do this.  See Approve ATC Exemptions.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-15\nValid as Of: 2024-11-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2411\n\n--- Record 1917 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Approve ATC Exemptions App: Replication of ATC Exemptions from On-Premise Towards SAP BTP\nDescription: You can now replicate ATC exemptions from your on-premise ATC system to the ATC in SAP BTP. Customers need to use transaction SATC_EXPORT_XMPT to download the exemptions from an on-premise ATC system.  See Enable Usage of the Approve ATC Exemptions App.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-15\nValid as Of: 2024-11-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2411\n\n--- Record 1918 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Automated Handling for Default Client Certificates\nDescription: SAP BTP ABAP environment tenants are now equipped with a signed default client certificate, which is automatically rotated and can be used for customer managed integration scenarios.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-15\nValid as Of: 2024-11-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2411\n\n--- Record 1919 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Business Event Logging\nDescription: With Business Event Logging, you can capture and log business events locally within the ABAP environment. It includes:      The business event log: A persistence of raised business events in the ABAP system.      The Activate Business Event Logging configuration item to activate logging on an object level.      UI apps to view the business event log.      CDS views to access the business event logs.      Communication scenario SAP_COM_0A54 to externally access and replicate data to other applications.     \",1208\n368,\"--- Record 2421 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Creating CDS Aspects in ABAP CDS Syntax\nDescription: You can now create CDS aspects to store field definitions and calculations, such as CDS expressions, in order to reuse them in other data definitions.  See Creating CDS Aspects.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2422 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Creating Logical External Schemas\nDescription: You can now create logical external schemas that can be used in combination with external entities for establishing outbound SQL access.  See Working with Logical External Schemas.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: nan\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2423 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Display Warnings Sent by SAP HANA\nDescription: When debugging a development object in which ABAP Managed Database Procedures (AMDP) are nested, the AMDP Debugger now displays warnings that are sent by the SAP HANA database.  See Stepping in AMDP Debugger.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2424 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Field Extension Wizard\nDescription: You can now use the field extension wizard to create extension fields.  See Generating Extension Fields.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2425 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Generating an ABAP CDS Provider Model\nDescription: The Generate ABAP Repository Objects Wizard creates ABAP development objects based on the Core Schema Notation model workbench object. It generates DDIC tables, CDS views, metadata extensions, and service definitions.  See Generating an ABAP CDS Provider Model with the Generate ABAP Repository Objects Wizard.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2426 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Maintain Baseline in the Custom Code Migration App\nDescription: You can now use the feature of adding findings to the baseline in the Custom Code Migration app.  See Custom Code Migration.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2427 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: New Feature Explorer Tour for RAP Business Object Tooling\nDescription: The new RAP BO tools tour has been added to the Feature Explorer. The tour allows you to learn more about the different features that are available for RAP BO development.  See Feature Explorer.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2428 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Opening Non-Native-Integrated Development Objects\nDescription: If you open an ABAP development object that is not native-integrated in Eclipse, it will now be opened in a new fallback editor in ADT. This editor shows, for example, the information that is usually displayed in the Properties view or the source code in a read-only preview.  See Opening Non-Native-Integrated Development Objects.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2429 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Planned Decommissioning Date for Deprecated Objects\nDescription: For formerly released but meanwhile deprecated local APIs, the system now shows their planned decommissioning date. If SAP has no concrete plans to change the state of an object to decommissioned, the date is not set, and the priorities of the corresponding ATC check results (developer extensibility) and rework tasks (key user extensibility) are lower than for objects with a planned decommissioning date. This will help you to prioritize the rework of custom objects that use deprecated APIs.  See Deprecation.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business:\",1208\n663,\"--- Record 841 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: RAP Business Objects Test Double Framework: Supported EML Statements\nDescription: The RAP Business Objects test double framework now supports these EML statements: Get Permissions, Key Functions and Set Locks.  See Writing Tests with Mock EML APIs Support.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: nan\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-16\nValid as Of: 2025-05-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2505\n\n--- Record 842 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Restructuring the \"\"Code Completion\"\" and \"\"Source Code Editors\"\" Preference Pages\nDescription: Some checkboxes and radio buttons on the Code Completion and Source Code Editors preference pages have been revised and relocated between the two pages. Additionally, the wording of some items and section titles has been revised. These changes enhance the usability and user experience when configuring preferences for code completion.  See:     Keyword Completion      Non-Keyword Completion      Using Automatic Code Completion      Inserting a Full Signature Automatically      Inserting or Overwriting Source Code      Closing Brackets and Literals Automatically    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-16\nValid as Of: 2025-05-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2505\n\n--- Record 843 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Supporting 'Between' Capabilities\nDescription: Data Preview now supports ‘between’ capabilities in the filter options.  See Using the Add Filter Button.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: nan\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-16\nValid as Of: 2025-05-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2505\n\n--- Record 844 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Testing Web API-Based Services Using Swagger UI\nDescription: You can now test Web API-based services from service binding using Swagger UI.  See Using Service Binding Editor for OData V2 Service.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: nan\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-16\nValid as Of: 2025-05-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2505\n\n--- Record 845 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Working with the Log When Migrating CDS DDIC-Based Views to CDS View Entities\nDescription: After finishing the simulation or migration of CDS DDIC-based views to CDS view entities, you can now filter the log on the result page using the Show Objects drop-down list box. These options enhance readability by limiting the number of displayed results.  In addition, you can now rerun a simulation or migration. This helps you to restart the process for a set of CDS DDIC-based views at the beginning. For example, you can trigger the productive migration from the result page of a simulation.  See Migrating CDS DDIC-Based Views to CDS View Entities.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-16\nValid as Of: 2025-05-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2505\n\n--- Record 846 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Custom Business Configurations: Intent Navigation\nDescription: If all technical key fields are provided as parameters to uniquely identify a record of an object page or subobject page, it's opened directly.See Custom Business Configurations App.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-16\nValid as Of: 2025-05-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2505\n\n--- Record 847 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Custom Code Analysis: 3-Tier Model ATC Checks\nDescription: There are now two new ATC checks of category 3-Tier Model: \"\"Usage of APIs\"\" and \"\"Allowed Enhancement Technologies\"\".  \"\"Usage of APIs\"\" verifies the usage of classic Tier 2 and Tier 3 ABAP development objects based on the usage guidelines of SAP APIs. It analyzes all ABAP development objects, except for those with ABAP language version \"\"Key User\"\" or \"\"ABAP Cloud Development\"\", by identifying their used APIs. For APIs that should not be used, the ATC check shares information on successors, if any.  \"\"Allowed Enhancement Technologies\"\" identifies whether only the BAdI enhancement technology has been used in the code.  Please update your allowed RFC function modules in your cloud connector accordingly. To do this, apply 2861842 .\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-16\nValid as Of: 2025-05-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2505\n\n--- Record 848 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Data Archiving: Storage Manager Implementation\nDescription: You can now use a new interface method to rollback faulty verified archive files.See Storage Manager Implementation.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-16\nValid as Of: \",1208\n299,\"--- Record 2411 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Deprecated Business Catalog for Analytical Queries\nDescription: The business catalog SAP_A4C_BC_DEV_PC used for the preview of analytical queries will be removed. Please use its successor BC SAP_A4C_BC_DEV_DAT_PRV_PC instead. Both business catalogs require the Developer business role.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2412 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Custom Business Configurations: Recreation of Variants Needed\nDescription: You need to recreate variants for the list report of the Fiori app Custom Business Configurations due to a change in the persistence key.  For more information, see SAP note: 3486327 .\nAction: Recommended\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2413 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: ABAP Debugger: Variables with Hidden Values\nDescription: In the ABAP Debugger, the variable values with a type that is based on the domains XUBCODE, RSECDATA or DISPLAY_PROTECTED_STRING/DISPLAY_PROTECTED_XSTRING, are now hidden in the Variables view and in the ABAP Internal Table (Debugger) view. The values, for example of passwords or other sensitive data, will then be displayed as ******** or DEADDA7A.  See Symbols with Hidden Content.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2414 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Assigning Fiori Space Templates to Business Role Templates\nDescription: You can now assign Fiori Space templates to business role templates. When a business role is created from a business role template, the related Fiori Spaces are assigned.  See Working with Business Role Template Launchpad Space Template Assignments.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2415 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: ATC Checks now Support List of Classic APIs\nDescription: Should released APIs for ABAP Cloud be missing, the ABAP Extensibility Guide recommends creating a custom API wrapper. The ATC checks “Usage of Released APIs” and “Usage of Released APIs (Cloudification Repository)”, which are classic APIs that are recommended to be used in a wrapper, were adjusted. If you're using a SAP BTP ABAP environment system as your central ATC check system, no ATC error is shown in case an API classified as classic is used in custom code. Instead, you’ll only receive a warning.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2416 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Browser for Cloudification Repository Content\nDescription: You can now browse through the content of the Cloudification Repository on GitHub.  See Cloudification Repository Viewer.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2417 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Communication Targets for HTTP Outbound Communication\nDescription: The usage of the new application destinations via outbound services of type communication target is recommended when developing a new application with HTTP outbound communication. This enables developers to define and control which applications can use a particular application destination.  See Working with Communication Targets.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2418 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Creating API Package Assignments\nDescription: You can now assign APIs to API packages. An API package assignment is a container that defines the assignment between the API package and the corresponding API object.  See Working with API Package Assignments.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2419 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Creating API Packages\nDescription: You can now create API packages. An API package is a container that can hold different types of APIs.  See\",1208\n66,\"--- Record 2891 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Application Job Catalog Entries Editor\nDescription: You can now display sections, groups, and parameters of application job catalog entries and synchronize the parameter list of the application job catalog entries with the corresponding ABAP class.  See Working with Application Job Catalog Entries.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-17\nValid as Of: 2024-05-17\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2405\n\n--- Record 2892 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: ATC Checks for Knowledge Transfer Documents\nDescription: There are now several ATC checks to ensure the quality of Knowledge Transfer Documents.  See Knowledge Transfer Documents.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-17\nValid as Of: 2024-05-17\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2405\n\n--- Record 2893 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Clear Console When Running an ABAP Application\nDescription: You now have the option to clear the console of previously displayed content when running an ABAP application in the ABAP development tools for Eclipse.  See  Running an ABAP Program (Console).\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-17\nValid as Of: 2024-05-17\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2405\n\n--- Record 2894 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Display Remote ATC Runs from SAP BTP in ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse\nDescription: It's now possible to display the results of an ATC mass run performed via theCustom Code Migration app in SAP BTP in the ATC result browser.  See  Working with the ATC Result Browser.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-15\nValid as Of: 2024-05-17\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2405\n\n--- Record 2895 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Displaying Failed Assertions and Status of Test Methods\nDescription: You can now display failed assertions and status of unit test methods directly in the source code editor.  See Evaluating ABAP Unit Test Results.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-17\nValid as Of: 2024-05-17\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2405\n\n--- Record 2896 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Exporting an ABAP Runtime Error as ZIP File\nDescription: You can now export short dumps as ZIP file on your local drive. This enables you to copy and share its content with your team or SAP.  To export, open the short dump in the ABAP Runtime Error viewer and choose the Export icon from the integrated toolbar and save it on the relevant drive.  See Exporting an ABAP Runtime Error as ZIP File.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-17\nValid as Of: 2024-05-17\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2405\n\n--- Record 2897 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Handling Issues Relating to Authorization Checks of Authorization Object S_DEVELOP\nDescription: The back-end and related APIs perform authorization checks in order to protect the ABAP Repository against unauthorized changes. Depending on the respective authorizations given to the respective role or user, this may result in error messages about missing authorizations.  Now, the authority checks are performed in a more consistent way.  See SAP note 3441852  Consistent use of the 'activity' in authorization checks against authorization object S_DEVELOP.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-17\nValid as Of: 2024-05-17\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2405\n\n--- Record 2898 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Improvements for Better Handling of Large ABAP Traces\nDescription: You can now minimize and restructure the number of levels how a call is displayed in the Aggregated Call Tree. Select the call in the Aggregated Call Tree and choose Set as New Root from the context menu. The call and the tree of its subsequent calls will then be displayed in a clear way.  See Analyzing Trace Events in the Aggregated Call Tree.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-17\nValid as Of: 2024-05-17\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2405\n\n--- Record 2899 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Launching ABAP Unit Tests with Quick Actions\nDescription: Using quick actions enables you to launch unit tests with a single mouse click. This can be used for single test methods\",1208\n369,\" plans to change the state of an object to decommissioned, the date is not set, and the priorities of the corresponding ATC check results (developer extensibility) and rework tasks (key user extensibility) are lower than for objects with a planned decommissioning date. This will help you to prioritize the rework of custom objects that use deprecated APIs.  See Deprecation.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2430 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Schedule Custom Code Analysis\nDescription: Through the Schedule Custom Code Analysis app, you can now schedule projects created in the Custom Code Migration app as application jobs. With this functionality, the analyses can be performed once or periodically. The Schedule Custom Code Analysis app is available to all users that have access to the Custom Code Migration app.  See Schedule Custom Code Analysis.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n\",1208\n\n\nOutput:\n", "role": "user"}], "parameters": {"model": "gpt-4o", "frequency_penalty": 0.0, "max_tokens": null, "n": 1, "presence_penalty": 0.0, "temperature": 0.0, "top_p": 1.0, "response_format": {"type": "json_object"}}}, "key": "chat_create_community_report_d75be9c89510db0e59f1288f720f7f68aaba8b8e04cd59ca2f8278ffbc7d4656_v2"}